The wisdom traditions, the religious traditions,

1574
01:08:01.510 --> 01:08:02.760
the indigenous traditions,

1575
01:08:02.760 --> 01:08:06.350
all knew that with biological puberty

1576
01:08:06.350 --> 01:08:10.130
and moving into middle and late adolescents,

1577
01:08:10.130 --> 01:08:13.360
there was as we change physically and look different,

1578
01:08:13.360 --> 01:08:15.160
we change spiritually.

1579
01:08:15.160 --> 01:08:15.993
They knew this.

1580
01:08:15.993 --> 01:08:17.860
And whether we're talking about Bar and Bat Mitzvah

1581
01:08:17.860 --> 01:08:19.770
for the (indistinct), the sweat lodge confirmation,

1582
01:08:19.770 --> 01:08:22.250
every tradition marks puberty as a time

1583
01:08:22.250 --> 01:08:23.660
of augmented spiritual awareness.

1584
01:08:23.660 --> 01:08:26.240
And they were met with rites of passage

1585
01:08:26.240 --> 01:08:30.500
to honor that and kind of anchor it.

1586
01:08:30.500 --> 01:08:33.890
Precisely and now we know to mirror that deep truth

1587
01:08:33.890 --> 01:08:36.690
of humanity through thousands of years.

1588
01:08:36.690 --> 01:08:38.720
That when we look through the lens of a twin study,

1589
01:08:38.720 --> 01:08:43.210
there's a 50% increase in the heritable contribution

1590
01:08:43.210 --> 01:08:45.010
going from middle to late adolescents

1591
01:08:45.010 --> 01:08:48.570
of spirituality with or without religion.

1592
01:08:48.570 --> 01:08:52.670
So whether or not there is a tradition

1593
01:08:52.670 --> 01:08:55.070
to greet the young adult coming of age,

1594
01:08:55.070 --> 01:08:56.790
whether or not there is a rite of passage

1595
01:08:56.790 --> 01:08:59.190
or a ceremony or a guide.

1596
01:08:59.190 --> 01:09:01.810
The young adult hungers for ultimate transcendence

1597
01:09:01.810 --> 01:09:02.740
and meaning.

1598
01:09:02.740 --> 01:09:06.560
Nagging questions of the head, desires of the heart

1599
01:09:06.560 --> 01:09:10.250
for connection, love, illumination, this happens.

1600
01:09:10.250 --> 01:09:13.450
But when we leave him or her out there willy nilly,

1601
01:09:13.450 --> 01:09:15.660
they're flailing, they're lost.

1602
01:09:15.660 --> 01:09:19.610
And what would be a hunt for transcendent truth

1603
01:09:19.610 --> 01:09:23.480
devolves into the cheap backdoor of transcendence

1604
01:09:23.480 --> 01:09:25.200
through addiction, right?

1605
01:09:25.200 --> 01:09:28.667
I get lots of emails from young adults who say,

1606
01:09:28.667 --> 01:09:30.770
"I was looking for transcendence.

1607
01:09:30.770 --> 01:09:33.810
I was looking for that sense of love and buoyancy.

1608
01:09:33.810 --> 01:09:35.860
And I took the tricky back door.

1609
01:09:35.860 --> 01:09:37.390
And at first it felt great.

1610
01:09:37.390 --> 01:09:39.490
And then I slid further and further down."

1611
01:09:40.810 --> 01:09:42.343
Young adults know what this is.

1612
01:09:42.343 --> 01:09:47.343
I mean, you've mentioned that the awakened brain

1613
01:09:48.330 --> 01:09:51.620
and depression are kind of two sides of the same coin

1614
01:09:51.620 --> 01:09:55.080
but what you just mentioned reminds me that

1615
01:09:56.310 --> 01:09:58.310
addiction is part of that as well.

1616
01:09:58.310 --> 01:10:02.160
It is a flip side and you hear long time in recovery

1617
01:10:02.160 --> 01:10:05.290
and there's this sort of adage or trope

1618
01:10:05.290 --> 01:10:10.050
in the recovery community that the addict

1619
01:10:10.050 --> 01:10:11.950
is the spiritual seeker.

1620
01:10:11.950 --> 01:10:14.880
They're just seeking for those answers in unhealthy ways.

1621
01:10:14.880 --> 01:10:17.410
But ultimately it's that emptiness,

1622
01:10:17.410 --> 01:10:20.250
that hole in the soul that yearning that leads them

1623
01:10:20.250 --> 01:10:23.570
towards drugs and alcohol as salve

1624
01:10:23.570 --> 01:10:27.740
or as a vehicle for a different state of consciousness

1625
01:10:27.740 --> 01:10:30.950
to tap into something that has meaning

1626
01:10:30.950 --> 01:10:33.180
outside of individuality.

1627
01:10:33.180 --> 01:10:35.080
And so can we show up honestly

1628
01:10:35.080 --> 01:10:39.240
for the team in the young adult and say, "I get it.

1629
01:10:39.240 --> 01:10:41.820
I appreciate the hunger for transcendence.

1630
01:10:41.820 --> 01:10:43.440
That warmth, that felt of buoyant,

1631
01:10:43.440 --> 01:10:45.940
that almost had fence of numinousness you can almost see.

1632
01:10:45.940 --> 01:10:47.980
That warmth, the joy."

1633
01:10:47.980 --> 01:10:50.720
In our day it was the lit lighters at a concert

1634
01:10:50.720 --> 01:10:52.210
the whole room had a glow.

1635
01:10:52.210 --> 01:10:53.310
And we felt like we were one.

1636
01:10:53.310 --> 01:10:55.470
This fence of being one.

1637
01:10:55.470 --> 01:10:56.530
I get it.

1638
01:10:56.530 --> 01:11:01.170
But do you still feel it the next day?

1639
01:11:01.170 --> 01:11:02.770
It felt so great last night.

1640
01:11:02.770 --> 01:11:05.050
It felt so connected last night when you were using,

1641
01:11:05.050 --> 01:11:06.510
but do you still feel it today

1642
01:11:06.510 --> 01:11:09.290
or was it sort of a false way in?

1643
01:11:09.290 --> 01:11:12.990
And I think that we need to honor the transcendent hunt

1644
01:11:14.170 --> 01:11:15.650
and support the transcendent hunt.

1645
01:11:15.650 --> 01:11:17.770
Because when we don't the young adult go shopping

1646
01:11:17.770 --> 01:11:21.290
and it can be the false sense of connection

1647
01:11:21.290 --> 01:11:22.610
through using drugs and alcohol.

1648
01:11:22.610 --> 01:11:24.450
It can also be that going shopping means

1649
01:11:24.450 --> 01:11:26.540
they find bad teachers.

1650
01:11:26.540 --> 01:11:29.310
And a lot of things that end up looking like extremism

1651
01:11:29.310 --> 01:11:31.380
or even terrorism are the young adults

1652
01:11:31.380 --> 01:11:33.283
shopping for a spiritual teacher.

1653
01:11:34.580 --> 01:11:35.470
We've got to show up,

1654
01:11:35.470 --> 01:11:37.130
we've got to know this is coming.

1655
01:11:37.130 --> 01:11:39.770
Hardwired, boot it up, look at it through twin studies.

1656
01:11:39.770 --> 01:11:42.670
It is absolutely a fact that with puberty

1657
01:11:42.670 --> 01:11:45.970
comes spiritual growth, spiritual hunger.

1658
01:11:45.970 --> 01:11:49.070
And the extent to which we support as adults

1659
01:11:49.070 --> 01:11:50.700
the formation of the spiritual course

1660
01:11:50.700 --> 01:11:52.240
extent to which that young adult

1661
01:11:52.240 --> 01:11:55.420
is protected against addiction and depression going forward.

1662
01:11:55.420 --> 01:11:57.823
Right, so extensively what you're saying is,

1663
01:11:58.710 --> 01:12:02.810
with this explosion in adolescent depression

1664
01:12:02.810 --> 01:12:05.500
and addiction rates going through the roof.

1665
01:12:05.500 --> 01:12:09.870
That part of the antidote or the treatment protocol

1666
01:12:09.870 --> 01:12:13.440
has to be cultivation of spiritual awareness

1667
01:12:13.440 --> 01:12:16.530
to take people through some protocol

1668
01:12:16.530 --> 01:12:19.580
where they can connect with their awakened brain

1669
01:12:19.580 --> 01:12:24.510
in some way to ameliorate or combat

1670
01:12:24.510 --> 01:12:27.190
the instincts that are leading

1671
01:12:27.190 --> 01:12:28.990
towards this mental health crisis

1672
01:12:28.990 --> 01:12:31.340
that we're contending with.

1673
01:12:31.340 --> 01:12:34.790
And if we do it's a set up for life.

1674
01:12:34.790 --> 01:12:37.440
The formative work of late adolescence,

1675
01:12:37.440 --> 01:12:40.253
the initial depression, if you will, sophomore slump.

1676
01:12:41.430 --> 01:12:44.473
Go back to being a sophomore if you can bear it, okay.

1677
01:12:44.473 --> 01:12:45.570
(Lisa laughing)

1678
01:12:45.570 --> 01:12:46.403
And I think-

1679
01:12:46.403 --> 01:12:47.236
Sophomore in college or high school?

1680
01:12:47.236 --> 01:12:49.297
Sophomore in college, sophomore in college.

1681
01:12:50.380 --> 01:12:51.810
So I invite everybody to think about

1682
01:12:51.810 --> 01:12:55.083
being a sophomore in college and not I'll go first.

1683
01:12:56.020 --> 01:12:58.880
I was a sophomore in college and I'd come to college

1684
01:12:58.880 --> 01:12:59.882
so confident.

1685
01:12:59.882 --> 01:13:02.470
And my mother loved me and my father loved me.

1686
01:13:02.470 --> 01:13:04.850
And I had great friends from growing up.

1687
01:13:04.850 --> 01:13:08.760
So I got to college and the greatest time I went to parties,

1688
01:13:08.760 --> 01:13:10.960
I was dancing and everything was fabulous.

1689
01:13:10.960 --> 01:13:13.127
And I met my first boyfriend and I thought,

1690
01:13:13.127 --> 01:13:14.270
"Oh, he's so funny.

1691
01:13:14.270 --> 01:13:15.103
He's so smart.

1692
01:13:15.103 --> 01:13:16.730
I've never met anyone so interesting.

1693
01:13:16.730 --> 01:13:17.563
He's a wrestler.

1694
01:13:17.563 --> 01:13:18.483
He's so beautiful.

1695
01:13:19.690 --> 01:13:21.291
He must really love me."

1696
01:13:21.291 --> 01:13:22.124
(Lisa chuckles)

1697
01:13:22.124 --> 01:13:22.957
And he said, he loved me.

1698
01:13:22.957 --> 01:13:23.900
And it was wonderful.

1699
01:13:23.900 --> 01:13:25.370
And we went out for a few months

1700
01:13:25.370 --> 01:13:26.587
but then he broke up with me.

1701
01:13:26.587 --> 01:13:27.770
And I couldn't believe it.

1702
01:13:27.770 --> 01:13:30.360
I said, "Wait, you said you loved me

1703
01:13:30.360 --> 01:13:32.020
and now you don't love me anymore?"

1704
01:13:32.020 --> 01:13:34.300
He's like, "No, I truly loved you.

1705
01:13:34.300 --> 01:13:37.148
I truly did and I just don't feel that now."

1706
01:13:37.148 --> 01:13:39.820
I'm like, "Well, how could you have loved me in November

1707
01:13:39.820 --> 01:13:41.730
but not love me in February?

1708
01:13:41.730 --> 01:13:42.990
How could that be?"

1709
01:13:42.990 --> 01:13:46.210
And also how could I not be lovable?

1710
01:13:46.210 --> 01:13:48.227
I mean, my mother loves me and my father loves me

1711
01:13:48.227 --> 01:13:49.610
and my best friends...

1712
01:13:49.610 --> 01:13:54.410
And it set me downward spiraling into this existential quest

1713
01:13:55.340 --> 01:13:57.520
that I now understand through science

1714
01:13:57.520 --> 01:14:00.140
every 20 year old is primed to have.

1715
01:14:00.140 --> 01:14:02.410
The trigger was that my heart was broken.

1716
01:14:02.410 --> 01:14:05.150
It was my first terrible breakup.

1717
01:14:05.150 --> 01:14:09.343
But the landing was into this deep existential pit.

1718
01:14:10.200 --> 01:14:13.167
And I thought, "Well, if we can love each other one day

1719
01:14:13.167 --> 01:14:16.500
and not the next then love isn't permanent.

1720
01:14:16.500 --> 01:14:19.110
So if love isn't permanent love isn't real."

1721
01:14:19.110 --> 01:14:21.530
And actually, I'll call this fellow Jason.

1722
01:14:21.530 --> 01:14:24.200
If Jason loved me one day and Jason doesn't the next,

1723
01:14:24.200 --> 01:14:25.640
then is there really a Jason?

1724
01:14:25.640 --> 01:14:26.860
Is Jason stable?

1725
01:14:26.860 --> 01:14:29.100
And this is the type of existential wondering

1726
01:14:29.100 --> 01:14:31.550
that the sophomore runs with.

1727
01:14:31.550 --> 01:14:34.580
Now some are more prone towards than others.

1728
01:14:34.580 --> 01:14:37.200
But these felt sense of here today gone tomorrow

1729
01:14:38.080 --> 01:14:39.920
leads to a form of struggling.

1730
01:14:39.920 --> 01:14:41.940
And I share in The Awakened Brain,

1731
01:14:41.940 --> 01:14:43.450
sophomore year I ended up

1732
01:14:43.450 --> 01:14:45.670
in the basement of my dorm at Yale.

1733
01:14:45.670 --> 01:14:48.550
Literally in the basement because in the freezing cold

1734
01:14:48.550 --> 01:14:50.160
of New Haven in the winter,

1735
01:14:50.160 --> 01:14:52.660
there was a hot water boiler in the basement

1736
01:14:52.660 --> 01:14:53.960
that it was at least warm.

1737
01:14:53.960 --> 01:14:56.490
And I could sit there all night by the hot water boiler

1738
01:14:56.490 --> 01:14:58.860
and wonder, "Well, does life have permanence?

1739
01:14:58.860 --> 01:15:00.670
And is there meaning written into life?"

1740
01:15:00.670 --> 01:15:04.410
And this reached the point which is actually normative.

1741
01:15:04.410 --> 01:15:05.390
Does God exist?

1742
01:15:05.390 --> 01:15:08.790
I mean, I'd grown up feeling God's presence my whole life

1743
01:15:08.790 --> 01:15:11.870
and my mother cries at the presence of God.

1744
01:15:11.870 --> 01:15:15.170
But does God exist because Jason broke up with me?

1745
01:15:15.170 --> 01:15:17.700
And that is the type of thing that psychotherapists

1746
01:15:17.700 --> 01:15:18.700
on college campuses.

1747
01:15:20.332 --> 01:15:23.090
Or psychotherapists that work with young adults in general

1748
01:15:23.090 --> 01:15:26.810
need to understand doesn't really have an answer

1749
01:15:26.810 --> 01:15:31.070
in negotiating our relationships interpersonally.

1750
01:15:31.070 --> 01:15:33.570
Doesn't really have an answer and identity work.

1751
01:15:33.570 --> 01:15:36.730
Doesn't really have an answer through the lens of the DSM

1752
01:15:36.730 --> 01:15:38.420
as an adult adjustment disorder

1753
01:15:38.420 --> 01:15:41.440
or some sort of moderate level major depression.

1754
01:15:41.440 --> 01:15:43.720
That is a grappling with existential truth

1755
01:15:43.720 --> 01:15:45.720
for which we are hardwired.

1756
01:15:45.720 --> 01:15:48.070
The trigger differs from person to person.

1757
01:15:48.070 --> 01:15:49.350
But wondering what is real?

1758
01:15:49.350 --> 01:15:50.183
What is true?

1759
01:15:50.183 --> 01:15:51.016
Is there good and evil?

1760
01:15:51.016 --> 01:15:51.849
Does love exist?

1761
01:15:51.849 --> 01:15:52.682
Does God exist?

1762
01:15:52.682 --> 01:15:53.515
Do I matter?

1763
01:15:53.515 --> 01:15:55.060
Does Jason matter?

1764
01:15:55.060 --> 01:15:59.720
That we are built to do and with that process,

1765
01:15:59.720 --> 01:16:02.777
there is a hunger to know the deepest nature of life

1766
01:16:02.777 --> 01:16:05.440
and the depression in not knowing the answer.

1767
01:16:05.440 --> 01:16:07.640
Yeah, I wonder whether that process

1768
01:16:07.640 --> 01:16:10.100
is precipitated more commonly these days

1769
01:16:10.100 --> 01:16:13.040
by a more profound sense of despair,

1770
01:16:13.040 --> 01:16:14.630
rather than my mother loved me

1771
01:16:14.630 --> 01:16:17.130
and why am I not lovable to him?

1772
01:16:17.130 --> 01:16:21.880
Isn't it more typical that the young individual

1773
01:16:21.880 --> 01:16:26.040
is repeating this narrative of I'm entirely unlovable?

1774
01:16:26.040 --> 01:16:28.710
Or I look terrible and I hate my body

1775
01:16:28.710 --> 01:16:30.050
and I can't make friends.

1776
01:16:30.050 --> 01:16:33.520
It's more of a darker disposition

1777
01:16:36.250 --> 01:16:39.220
that is much more kind of dire.

1778
01:16:39.220 --> 01:16:43.700
Yes and also mom and dad you say you love me,

1779
01:16:43.700 --> 01:16:46.450
but you're handing me a world

1780
01:16:46.450 --> 01:16:48.530
that's on the edge of environmental collapse.

1781
01:16:48.530 --> 01:16:51.860
Or my teachers say they know things,

1782
01:16:51.860 --> 01:16:53.660
but they're handed me a world

1783
01:16:53.660 --> 01:16:57.670
that's full of political rifts and immature behavior

1784
01:16:57.670 --> 01:16:59.020
amongst adults.

1785
01:16:59.020 --> 01:17:01.090
So what...

1786
01:17:01.090 --> 01:17:05.560
And I think that the answer is in the young adult.

1787
01:17:05.560 --> 01:17:07.970
But it's not in the way that we're talking to them now.

1788
01:17:07.970 --> 01:17:10.940
We need a new way of thinking and a new way of engaging

1789
01:17:10.940 --> 01:17:11.773
the young adult.

1790
01:17:12.720 --> 01:17:14.690
And that way it looks like what?

1791
01:17:14.690 --> 01:17:18.410
And that way is you say you can't stand your body.

1792
01:17:18.410 --> 01:17:21.140
You say I love you but I wasn't there

1793
01:17:21.140 --> 01:17:23.710
in the way you wish I was there for you.

1794
01:17:23.710 --> 01:17:27.393
Let's connect with the deepest truest part of yourself.

1795
01:17:28.360 --> 01:17:31.830
I invite you to connect into the deepest place

1796
01:17:31.830 --> 01:17:35.230
of your inner wisdom from which you can start to receive

1797
01:17:35.230 --> 01:17:40.230
and perceive direct awareness of the yellow door

1798
01:17:40.393 --> 01:17:42.070
of a way forward.

1799
01:17:42.070 --> 01:17:46.770
We have shut out the young adult from her or his resource

1800
01:17:46.770 --> 01:17:48.610
for recovery and renewal.

1801
01:17:48.610 --> 01:17:51.320
We have locked them out of the kingdom

1802
01:17:51.320 --> 01:17:53.300
and all it takes is the key to get back in.

1803
01:17:53.300 --> 01:17:55.810
They have it and we can help them do that.

1804
01:17:55.810 --> 01:17:57.520
We can help them reawaken.

1805
01:17:57.520 --> 01:17:59.600
We can help them ignite their...

1806
01:17:59.600 --> 01:18:00.970
I call it awakened awareness.

1807
01:18:00.970 --> 01:18:02.490
Their seat of transcendent awareness

1808
01:18:02.490 --> 01:18:06.600
where they can feel direct connection to this pulse of life.

1809
01:18:06.600 --> 01:18:07.960
And that can be taught.

1810
01:18:07.960 --> 01:18:10.390
I mean, honoring our inner knowing,

1811
01:18:10.390 --> 01:18:13.020
connecting as we just did in our visualization

1812
01:18:13.020 --> 01:18:15.560
with those who truly have our best interest in mind.

1813
01:18:15.560 --> 01:18:18.720
It could be a grandparent who died 20 years ago, right?

1814
01:18:18.720 --> 01:18:20.650
It has to do with talking directly to God

1815
01:18:20.650 --> 01:18:22.870
or feeling, asking the universe of question

1816
01:18:22.870 --> 01:18:24.820
and hearing the answer.

1817
01:18:24.820 --> 01:18:26.630
Whether it's through my mind's eye

1818
01:18:26.630 --> 01:18:28.690
and my relationship with my higher power?

1819
01:18:28.690 --> 01:18:30.090
Whether it's through synchronicity?

1820
01:18:30.090 --> 01:18:31.470
Whether it's through the care of the geese

1821
01:18:31.470 --> 01:18:33.020
or the duck or the wind?

1822
01:18:33.020 --> 01:18:36.500
Being able to see life as a live and guiding.

1823
01:18:36.500 --> 01:18:37.333
We're built for that.

1824
01:18:37.333 --> 01:18:39.910
That's not a belief it's not a theology.

1825
01:18:39.910 --> 01:18:42.270
That doesn't come from a religious leader.

1826
01:18:42.270 --> 01:18:43.587
That comes from a scientist saying,

1827
01:18:43.587 --> 01:18:47.740
"That we have in our brain a series of circuits

1828
01:18:47.740 --> 01:18:51.570
that allow us to see the deep nature of life.

1829
01:18:51.570 --> 01:18:53.000
That is in fact buoyant.

1830
01:18:53.000 --> 01:18:55.210
That is in fact a consciousness field

1831
01:18:55.210 --> 01:18:59.260
through which we are loved, held, guided and never alone."

1832
01:18:59.260 --> 01:19:01.170
And so on a very practical level,

1833
01:19:01.170 --> 01:19:03.970
if there's a parent listening to this who's dealing with

1834
01:19:04.850 --> 01:19:09.190
one of their adolescents who's struggling at the moment.

1835
01:19:09.190 --> 01:19:13.390
What are some of the practices or tools that you can relate

1836
01:19:13.390 --> 01:19:16.080
that could be conveyed to this young person

1837
01:19:16.080 --> 01:19:17.647
to help in that process?

1838
01:19:17.647 --> 01:19:20.510
Right, I'll answer very concrete things we can do.

1839
01:19:20.510 --> 01:19:22.470
First of all, our young adults

1840
01:19:22.470 --> 01:19:26.190
as much as they may be rebelling and pushing us away,

1841
01:19:26.190 --> 01:19:30.117
don't want us to even see them listening to us, right?

1842
01:19:31.071 --> 01:19:32.510
But remember every word we say

1843
01:19:32.510 --> 01:19:34.810
when we speak from our deepest truth.

1844
01:19:34.810 --> 01:19:37.760
So if I can tell the story of sitting in the basement

1845
01:19:37.760 --> 01:19:41.080
of my dorm in college and wondering if God exists?

1846
01:19:41.080 --> 01:19:44.370
But then going that summer to the Gulf of Mexico

1847
01:19:44.370 --> 01:19:46.580
and seeing light on the water

1848
01:19:46.580 --> 01:19:49.740
and not radically hitting my head against the wall,

1849
01:19:49.740 --> 01:19:54.150
ruminating asking if God exist but in that moment feeling.

1850
01:19:54.150 --> 01:19:56.500
And then of course, God exists.

1851
01:19:56.500 --> 01:19:59.590
Knowing in a deeper, direct way.

1852
01:19:59.590 --> 01:20:02.490
Of course, we are held and loved.

1853
01:20:02.490 --> 01:20:05.480
But deep awakening in our own paths.

1854
01:20:05.480 --> 01:20:06.990
Our children will listen to every word.

1855
01:20:06.990 --> 01:20:08.530
I'll give you an example.

1856
01:20:08.530 --> 01:20:09.850
When I was a child,

1857
01:20:09.850 --> 01:20:12.850
my mother was very profoundly spiritually connected.

1858
01:20:12.850 --> 01:20:16.140
Very vocal about her spiritual life.

1859
01:20:16.140 --> 01:20:19.257
Prayed out loud, cried at the side of my brother and I.

1860
01:20:19.257 --> 01:20:20.740
"Thank you God for these children.

1861
01:20:20.740 --> 01:20:22.639
Thank you God for the sunset."

1862
01:20:22.639 --> 01:20:23.472
Hallelu...

1863
01:20:23.472 --> 01:20:24.760
And just full of life.

1864
01:20:24.760 --> 01:20:29.340
And my father was a very quiet, reflective academic

1865
01:20:29.340 --> 01:20:32.040
who would read on the back porch and was very cautious

1866
01:20:32.040 --> 01:20:34.623
in making any assertions about spiritual life.

1867
01:20:35.830 --> 01:20:39.470
But it was my father who the very morning

1868
01:20:39.470 --> 01:20:40.883
after his mother died.

1869
01:20:42.220 --> 01:20:44.730
I was about nine years old.

1870
01:20:44.730 --> 01:20:47.330
I woke up as I always did at 4:00 AM,

1871
01:20:47.330 --> 01:20:51.080
went downstairs but I was very surprised that morning

1872
01:20:51.080 --> 01:20:52.573
to see my father almost in a ball.

1873
01:20:52.573 --> 01:20:55.210
Because my father is 6'5" handsome guy,

1874
01:20:55.210 --> 01:20:56.050
basketball player...

1875
01:20:56.050 --> 01:21:00.340
In a little ball on the carpet by our living room couch.

1876
01:21:00.340 --> 01:21:02.040
And I walked to him I said, "Dad."

1877
01:21:02.920 --> 01:21:05.150
And he said, "I had a dream."

1878
01:21:05.150 --> 01:21:09.467
This was within 24 hours of his own mother's passing.

1879
01:21:09.467 --> 01:21:11.783
"Grandma came to me in my dream.

1880
01:21:12.960 --> 01:21:14.700
And where's grandma loved to dress up

1881
01:21:14.700 --> 01:21:16.690
and wear pretty clothes and jewelry.

1882
01:21:16.690 --> 01:21:20.790
In this dream grandma's in a very everyday gray suit.

1883
01:21:20.790 --> 01:21:23.373
It was a suit I saw her wear many times.

1884
01:21:24.570 --> 01:21:28.240
And there grandma and I were walking down Grand Avenue."

1885
01:21:28.240 --> 01:21:30.493
In Des Moines, Iowa, where my father grew up.

1886
01:21:32.050 --> 01:21:33.946
And he said, "You know...

1887
01:21:33.946 --> 01:21:37.260
And it was very raw and he certainly was not philosophizing

1888
01:21:37.260 --> 01:21:39.280
it was just real as could be.

1889
01:21:39.280 --> 01:21:42.520
He said, "You know, I don't know what to make of it

1890
01:21:42.520 --> 01:21:45.900
but I guess it means that grandma

1891
01:21:45.900 --> 01:21:48.430
had always walked with me as my mother.

1892
01:21:48.430 --> 01:21:50.860
She would continue to walk with me as my mother

1893
01:21:51.700 --> 01:21:53.800
and the grandma was letting me know that."

1894
01:21:55.650 --> 01:22:00.440
Okay, so fast forward I'm decades down the road.

1895
01:22:00.440 --> 01:22:03.390
When I think of my father and the depth of our relationship,

1896
01:22:03.390 --> 01:22:04.800
I go there.

1897
01:22:04.800 --> 01:22:08.100
When I think do our ancestors walk with us, I go there,

1898
01:22:08.100 --> 01:22:10.710
I've published reams of articles showing that in India

1899
01:22:10.710 --> 01:22:11.840
and in China and Mexico,

1900
01:22:11.840 --> 01:22:14.320
there's a deep awareness that ancestors walk with us.

1901
01:22:14.320 --> 01:22:15.870
I've published reams of articles showing that

1902
01:22:15.870 --> 01:22:18.610
when we know that we're less depressed and addicted.

1903
01:22:18.610 --> 01:22:21.150
But I know it's true that our ancestors walk with us

1904
01:22:21.150 --> 01:22:23.213
because my father shared his dream.

1905
01:22:23.213 --> 01:22:27.690
I had 100% proof of concept, hard data,

1906
01:22:27.690 --> 01:22:31.370
in the felt awareness of that very awakened bond.

1907
01:22:31.370 --> 01:22:32.296
That was real.

1908
01:22:32.296 --> 01:22:33.690
Yeah, that's a beautiful story.

1909
01:22:33.690 --> 01:22:35.310
But that's who we are so yes.

1910
01:22:35.310 --> 01:22:37.610
And the fact that it came in the form of your dad,

1911
01:22:37.610 --> 01:22:39.780
the unlikely kind of spiritual seeker

1912
01:22:39.780 --> 01:22:41.700
in comparison to your mom.

1913
01:22:41.700 --> 01:22:45.520
Which makes that story all the more kind of poignant, yeah.

1914
01:22:45.520 --> 01:22:49.190
And he didn't know what it meant in a theoretical

1915
01:22:49.190 --> 01:22:51.110
or theological sense.

1916
01:22:51.110 --> 01:22:55.620
It was 100% hard data because it was his genuine experience.

1917
01:22:55.620 --> 01:23:00.620
Sure, and yet it requires kind of reckoning.

1918
01:23:03.360 --> 01:23:06.690
Like I feel myself even like wanting to dismiss

1919
01:23:06.690 --> 01:23:08.080
those stories because there are all

1920
01:23:08.080 --> 01:23:10.070
sort of individual experiences

1921
01:23:10.070 --> 01:23:12.140
and who knows what's going on in people's brain,

1922
01:23:12.140 --> 01:23:13.560
neurochemistry of course.

1923
01:23:13.560 --> 01:23:15.050
In the wake of his mother dying

1924
01:23:15.050 --> 01:23:16.700
he's gonna be reflecting on that.

1925
01:23:16.700 --> 01:23:19.820
And it's not surprising that there would be

1926
01:23:19.820 --> 01:23:23.780
some kind of dream and we can just kind of dismiss it

1927
01:23:23.780 --> 01:23:25.680
and say, "Oh, that's cute or whatever."

1928
01:23:25.680 --> 01:23:28.280
But that's not necessarily real.

1929
01:23:28.280 --> 01:23:30.040
Well, and that's why we're depressed

1930
01:23:30.040 --> 01:23:33.070
is because we dismiss half our form of human knowing.

1931
01:23:33.070 --> 01:23:35.430
It is the part that's buoyant and loving and guiding,

1932
01:23:35.430 --> 01:23:36.783
and doesn't leave us alone.

1933
01:23:37.700 --> 01:23:38.907
So, you know-

1934
01:23:40.101 --> 01:23:40.934
But when it wants you to deal with something

1935
01:23:43.000 --> 01:23:44.640
I like the way I always think about it

1936
01:23:44.640 --> 01:23:47.780
is the universe is knocking on your door

1937
01:23:47.780 --> 01:23:49.070
and it knocks gently like,

1938
01:23:49.070 --> 01:23:51.370
Hey, I'm gonna give you a little dream,

1939
01:23:51.370 --> 01:23:52.230
maybe look at this.

1940
01:23:52.230 --> 01:23:55.250
Or there's gonna be some geese that are gonna fly above you.

1941
01:23:55.250 --> 01:23:56.527
Maybe you want to pay attention to that.

1942
01:23:56.527 --> 01:23:59.880
And every time that you dismiss it or refuse to look at it

1943
01:23:59.880 --> 01:24:02.720
or deny it the next Knocks a little louder,

1944
01:24:02.720 --> 01:24:04.560
the next Knocks a little louder,

1945
01:24:04.560 --> 01:24:07.460
until suddenly cops are involved in maybe jail

1946
01:24:07.460 --> 01:24:08.600
or a mental institution...

1947
01:24:08.600 --> 01:24:12.050
Like it just gets increasingly more and more intense

1948
01:24:12.050 --> 01:24:15.180
until finally you reach some inflection point

1949
01:24:15.180 --> 01:24:19.040
that entails a bunch of pain where you have no choice

1950
01:24:19.040 --> 01:24:22.380
but to look at the thing that had you paid attention

1951
01:24:22.380 --> 01:24:25.730
to it earlier on would have saved you a lot of consternation

1952
01:24:25.730 --> 01:24:26.763
and toil.

1953
01:24:27.910 --> 01:24:28.750
I agree with you.

1954
01:24:28.750 --> 01:24:32.000
The universe turns the volume up until we hear.

1955
01:24:32.000 --> 01:24:34.060
And so where are we trying to get?

1956
01:24:34.060 --> 01:24:36.680
We're trying to get as you described so beautifully

1957
01:24:36.680 --> 01:24:38.520
into a dialogue with life.

1958
01:24:38.520 --> 01:24:39.940
What is life showing me now?

1959
01:24:39.940 --> 01:24:42.460
What am I being told here, right?

1960
01:24:42.460 --> 01:24:44.330
So we don't step on an inert stage

1961
01:24:44.330 --> 01:24:46.250
where we control everything narrowly

1962
01:24:46.250 --> 01:24:47.790
what I call achieving awareness.

1963
01:24:47.790 --> 01:24:51.760
But we don't control the skies we navigate them, right?

1964
01:24:51.760 --> 01:24:52.593
We don't.

1965
01:24:52.593 --> 01:24:54.380
We'll get swallowed up in the waves of the ocean

1966
01:24:54.380 --> 01:24:55.660
if we think we're gonna control them.

1967
01:24:55.660 --> 01:24:57.670
If you get up on top and surf them.

1968
01:24:57.670 --> 01:25:01.490
That sense of being in a dynamic relationship

1969
01:25:01.490 --> 01:25:03.680
with the guidance spirit in life.

1970
01:25:03.680 --> 01:25:05.480
What is life showing me now?

1971
01:25:05.480 --> 01:25:08.420
Opens up a path that is one of discovery.

1972
01:25:08.420 --> 01:25:09.680
We don't make our way in life.

1973
01:25:09.680 --> 01:25:10.683
We discover our way in life.

1974
01:25:10.683 --> 01:25:12.230
I have no idea what my life's gonna look like

1975
01:25:12.230 --> 01:25:13.560
in 10 years.

1976
01:25:13.560 --> 01:25:16.330
But I know when I'm in a state of deep alignment

1977
01:25:16.330 --> 01:25:18.560
where I'm listening to life and life is opening doors.

1978
01:25:18.560 --> 01:25:20.404
And I know when I'm not.

1979
01:25:20.404 --> 01:25:21.237
When I'm not,

1980
01:25:21.237 --> 01:25:24.260
it's been both to my peril and everyone around me.

1981
01:25:24.260 --> 01:25:25.210
In other words,

1982
01:25:25.210 --> 01:25:28.223
there's a relinquishment of the instinct

1983
01:25:28.223 --> 01:25:33.223
to enforce yourself well and a reckoning

1984
01:25:34.050 --> 01:25:37.050
or a reconciliation with the idea of surrender

1985
01:25:37.050 --> 01:25:37.883
and acceptance.

1986
01:25:37.883 --> 01:25:40.290
It's more like surfing than it is like

1987
01:25:40.290 --> 01:25:42.500
pushing a rock up a mountain.

1988
01:25:42.500 --> 01:25:44.610
And this is the great dilemma

1989
01:25:44.610 --> 01:25:46.820
for every high achievement person, right?

1990
01:25:46.820 --> 01:25:49.430
Like you wanna force a result.

1991
01:25:49.430 --> 01:25:52.780
You have an addiction to a certain outcome

1992
01:25:52.780 --> 01:25:57.780
and our lives are directed towards increasingly becoming

1993
01:25:58.420 --> 01:26:00.930
sort of climbing this mountain towards achievement

1994
01:26:00.930 --> 01:26:03.310
or some imagined destination.

1995
01:26:03.310 --> 01:26:05.290
When in truth, the greatest miracles in life

1996
01:26:05.290 --> 01:26:06.979
and the greatest discoveries

1997
01:26:06.979 --> 01:26:11.320
and the experience of deep fulfillment and connection

1998
01:26:11.320 --> 01:26:14.100
comes with relinquishing all of that.

1999
01:26:14.100 --> 01:26:16.600
Letting go and being in the allowing.

2000
01:26:16.600 --> 01:26:19.190
But that requires synchronicity

2001
01:26:19.190 --> 01:26:21.850
with that invisible force, right?

2002
01:26:21.850 --> 01:26:26.177
You have to do enough inside work so that you are attuned

2003
01:26:27.140 --> 01:26:29.120
to those signals and presence enough

2004
01:26:29.120 --> 01:26:32.060
and integrated enough with who you are

2005
01:26:32.060 --> 01:26:35.430
so that you can be aware and act in accordance

2006
01:26:35.430 --> 01:26:38.063
with the signals that you're receiving

2007
01:26:38.063 --> 01:26:39.650
And synchronicity is-

2008
01:26:39.650 --> 01:26:42.170
And that's yeah, this is a whole synchronicity thing

2009
01:26:42.170 --> 01:26:43.700
that you talk about in the book.

2010
01:26:43.700 --> 01:26:45.330
That is a knock at the door.

2011
01:26:45.330 --> 01:26:50.330
That is one form of life talking to us now is synchronicity.

2012
01:26:50.710 --> 01:26:54.170
I love obviously like my first kind of passion

2013
01:26:54.170 --> 01:26:57.680
with all of this stuff is addiction and recovery.

2014
01:27:00.660 --> 01:27:05.490
And it's always interesting and at times quite frustrating

2015
01:27:05.490 --> 01:27:10.150
to have conversations about how to get sober

2016
01:27:10.150 --> 01:27:11.790
and what recovery looks like

2017
01:27:13.640 --> 01:27:17.790
because I'm basically somebody who got sober in AA

2018
01:27:17.790 --> 01:27:21.990
with a very traditional kind of rigor of the 12 steps.

2019
01:27:21.990 --> 01:27:25.910
And there's this sense that because a lot of the language

2020
01:27:25.910 --> 01:27:29.170
and the vernacular in the big book and all of that

2021
01:27:29.170 --> 01:27:31.980
is sort of antiquated and colloquial

2022
01:27:33.380 --> 01:27:37.060
that the spiritual piece in the 12 steps

2023
01:27:37.060 --> 01:27:39.160
is like the fly in the ointment

2024
01:27:39.160 --> 01:27:42.670
or a bug rather than a feature.

2025
01:27:42.670 --> 01:27:45.620
And anybody who's kind of gotten sober

2026
01:27:45.620 --> 01:27:47.450
or maintained sobriety through this program

2027
01:27:47.450 --> 01:27:50.800
understands that spirituality is at the very core

2028
01:27:50.800 --> 01:27:53.490
of what this experience is all about.

2029
01:27:53.490 --> 01:27:55.540
It's not something that's off to the side

2030
01:27:55.540 --> 01:27:57.620
or something that you can kind of choose

2031
01:27:57.620 --> 01:28:00.720
to not engage with while you do the rest of it.

2032
01:28:00.720 --> 01:28:03.670
And to my mind the work that you've done

2033
01:28:03.670 --> 01:28:08.670
and all the science that you've done over the years

2034
01:28:09.150 --> 01:28:11.373
really proves this out for me.

2035
01:28:12.260 --> 01:28:16.349
Like it validates this methodology.

2036
01:28:16.349 --> 01:28:21.349
I am so grateful indeed that this can be brought

2037
01:28:21.710 --> 01:28:23.370
to people who are overcoming

2038
01:28:23.370 --> 01:28:26.240
and being renewed in recovery.

2039
01:28:26.240 --> 01:28:27.773
Yeah, because people will say like,

2040
01:28:27.773 --> 01:28:28.817
"(indistinct) I go to AA

2041
01:28:28.817 --> 01:28:31.000
but I can't get down with the God thing

2042
01:28:31.000 --> 01:28:32.560
or I can't, you know, I'm not a religious (indistinct)."

2043
01:28:32.560 --> 01:28:34.670
It's not a religious program it's a spiritual program.

2044
01:28:34.670 --> 01:28:36.050
It's a God of your choosing.

2045
01:28:36.050 --> 01:28:37.840
Your higher power can be the group.

2046
01:28:37.840 --> 01:28:40.520
It can be anything you wanna to be.

2047
01:28:40.520 --> 01:28:43.570
But people and this is a big piece I think.

2048
01:28:43.570 --> 01:28:45.950
There's a lot of people who have spiritual trauma

2049
01:28:45.950 --> 01:28:48.690
or religious trauma because of some experience

2050
01:28:48.690 --> 01:28:50.770
when they were younger where

2051
01:28:50.770 --> 01:28:52.980
it doesn't necessarily have to be physical abuse,

2052
01:28:52.980 --> 01:28:57.030
but some level of bad experience occurred

2053
01:28:57.030 --> 01:29:00.160
in their relationship to anything spiritual

2054
01:29:00.160 --> 01:29:03.100
that a door comes down and they shut themselves off

2055
01:29:03.100 --> 01:29:04.303
from that completely.

2056
01:29:06.220 --> 01:29:10.010
That is a story I've heard from hundreds of people

2057
01:29:10.010 --> 01:29:14.250
that I was a very spiritual child, I felt connected.

2058
01:29:14.250 --> 01:29:16.380
I may be prayed through my faith tradition

2059
01:29:16.380 --> 01:29:19.470
or just felt in this deep loving numinous connection.

2060
01:29:19.470 --> 01:29:21.340
And then there was a bad messenger.

2061
01:29:21.340 --> 01:29:23.100
And the messenger could have been a little bit bad

2062
01:29:23.100 --> 01:29:24.510
or a lot bad.

2063
01:29:24.510 --> 01:29:28.470
But here she didn't walk the walk, right?

2064
01:29:28.470 --> 01:29:31.550
They talked the walk but they didn't walk the walk.

2065
01:29:31.550 --> 01:29:35.760
And when the young adult sees hypocrisy

2066
01:29:35.760 --> 01:29:40.040
or far worse as even violated by the messenger,

2067
01:29:40.040 --> 01:29:43.090
there's a tendency to throw the spiritual baby out

2068
01:29:43.090 --> 01:29:44.890
with the bath water, right?

2069
01:29:44.890 --> 01:29:47.820
And here's where our confusion

2070
01:29:47.820 --> 01:29:50.930
as a culture between religion and spirituality

2071
01:29:50.930 --> 01:29:52.120
is really at play.

2072
01:29:52.120 --> 01:29:55.670
We have a non conversant society around spirituality

2073
01:29:55.670 --> 01:29:58.920
and so much so that I will give a two hour talk

2074
01:29:58.920 --> 01:30:00.710
on the science of spirituality

2075
01:30:00.710 --> 01:30:02.560
as being distinct from religion.

2076
01:30:02.560 --> 01:30:04.407
And then out by the water cooler someone says,

2077
01:30:04.407 --> 01:30:05.410
"What's the difference again

2078
01:30:05.410 --> 01:30:06.840
between spirituality and religion?"

2079
01:30:06.840 --> 01:30:08.950
We're just turn deaf as a culture.

2080
01:30:08.950 --> 01:30:10.660
But they're two entirely different things.

2081
01:30:10.660 --> 01:30:12.760
Spirituality is in our innate capacity

2082
01:30:12.760 --> 01:30:14.630
for transcendent awareness through which we are

2083
01:30:14.630 --> 01:30:16.400
in touch with our higher power

2084
01:30:16.400 --> 01:30:18.650
or the goodness and spirit and then through one another.

2085
01:30:18.650 --> 01:30:21.677
AA is abundant with the presence of God or spirit

2086
01:30:21.677 --> 01:30:22.966
and in through one another.

2087
01:30:22.966 --> 01:30:25.070
(indistinct) the commitment, the humility,

2088
01:30:25.070 --> 01:30:26.440
the openhandedness.

2089
01:30:26.440 --> 01:30:27.273
Those relationships are-

2090
01:30:27.273 --> 01:30:28.350
